# Judge item J1811

Rate the finding: `real` (a real defect at head), `style`, `wrong`, or `not-a-finding`.

## Finding

``` text
head/evals/harness/execute-agent.sh:266 — The `rule_files` toggle never fails when the files it is meant to remove are absent: when neither stash-safety.md nor skill-invariants.md exists in the sandbox the loop records `removed: none present` and the trial continues with exit 0. The header (line 65) and both suite files promise that a toggle that cannot take effect is exit 2 so "an arm never silently runs as its baseline"; verified by running the no_rule_files arm against a prompt tree with no .claude/rules/ (exit 0, arm_evidence.rule_files = "removed: none present"). The pre-registered no_rule_files arm can therefore produce baseline results labelled as the control arm. Fail (return 2) when `gone` is empty, and add an arm-toggles.bats case for it alongside AT-9.
head/evals/harness/run-arms.sh:257 — Re-running the same batch name with the same source commit and model passes the guard on lines 251-255, rewrites MANIFEST.json (fixtures, arms, trials_planned, created) and starts the per-arm DONE/FAILED/PLANNED counters from zero, while `collect` appends to the existing `<arm>/results.jsonl`. STATUS.json then reports only the latest run's counts, MANIFEST.json describes only the latest run, but arms-report.py reads every accumulated row, so the three artefacts disagree about how many trials the batch holds. Either refuse a batch that already holds non-dry-run results (as the model/source mismatch case does) or seed the counters from the existing rows.
head/.claude/scripts/guard-y …
```

